Feature: Agent registry card
  The Agents API shows the Agent Card the gateway serves for a managed agent, as
  callers get it, and says how the gateway obtains it: fetched from the agent and
  rewritten, generated by an A2A proxy, or served by a remote gateway.

  Scenario: The card of an agent behind a URL Target is fetched and rewritten
    Given an A2A surface targeting managed agent "bravo"
    And managed agent "bravo" serves an Agent Card that names its own address
    And the operator has looked up the surface's agent
    When the operator reads the agent card of the surface's agent
    Then the admin API response status is 200
    And the agent card is available with source "fetched"
    And the agent card points at the gateway

  Scenario: The card of an agent behind an A2A proxy is generated by the proxy
    Given non-A2A managed agent "bravo" is available
    And A2A proxy "worker" targets non-A2A managed agent "bravo"
    And A2A surface "alpha" exists for route "/example" targeting A2A proxy "worker"
    And the operator has looked up the surface's agent
    When the operator reads the agent card of the surface's agent
    Then the admin API response status is 200
    And the agent card is available with source "generated"

  Scenario: The card of an agent whose surfaces aren't running is unavailable
    Given an A2A surface targeting managed agent "bravo"
    And the operator has looked up the surface's agent
    And the operator has disabled the stored surface
    When the operator reads the agent card of the surface's agent
    Then the admin API response status is 200
    And the agent card is unavailable because none of the agent's surfaces is running

  Scenario: The card read through a surface that isn't running is not found
    Given an A2A surface targeting managed agent "bravo"
    And the operator has looked up the surface's agent
    And the operator has disabled the stored surface
    When the operator reads the agent card of the surface's agent through that surface
    Then the admin API response status is 404
